+
+### `applyMergePatch(target, patch)`
+
+Applies a [JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386) (RFC 7386) to a target JSON
+document and returns the merged document as a new value; it does not mutate `target` or `patch`. A
+patch member set to `null` removes the corresponding member from the target; any other member is
+merged recursively if both sides are objects, or otherwise replaces the target's value wholesale
+(this includes arrays, which are always replaced rather than merged element-by-element). A patch that
+is not itself a JSON object (e.g. an array, a string, or `null`) replaces the whole target.
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+const document = { title: "Draft", tags: ["a", "b"], author: { name: "Alex" } };
+
+applyMergePatch(document, {
+  title: "Published",
+  tags: ["a", "b", "c"],
+  author: { email: null },
+}); // { title: "Published", tags: ["a", "b", "c"], author: { name: "Alex" } }
+```
